<article class="prose">
    <p class="muted">Last updated 19 August 2026.</p>

    <% if (locale !== 'en') { %>
    <p class="muted"><em><%= t('privacy.englishOnly') %></em></p>
    <% } %>
    <p>Weekly Budget is run by one person as a personal project. It has no
       advertising, no trackers and no third-party services. This page describes
       everything it does with your data, which is not much.</p>

    <h2>What is stored</h2>
    <p>Only what you type into it:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>The budget's name, weekly amount, and which weekday its week starts on.</li>
        <li>Each expense: description, amount, date, and category.</li>
        <li>Category names.</li>
        <li>A budget ID, generated on your device when you create a budget.</li>
        <li>Invitations you create: a random token, which budget it is for, when
            it was made, and when it was used. No record of who it was sent to,
            because the app never knows.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>That is the whole list. There are no accounts, so there is no email
       address, no password, no name, and no phone number. Nothing is collected
       about your device, your location, or your contacts, and nothing is used
       to build a profile of you.</p>

    <h2>Usage counts</h2>
    <p>To see whether the app is working and how much it is being used, the
       server keeps a daily tally of how many requests it handled, which screens
       or endpoints they were for, which app they came from (Android, iPhone or
       the website), and how many failed. These are counts only — one row per day
       per screen — and they are not tied to you, to a device, or to anything you
       typed.</p>
    <p>It also records which budgets were used on which day, so that "how many
       budgets are active" can be answered. That is a date and a budget ID and
       nothing else: no times, no list of what was done.</p>
    <p>No third party receives any of this. It is not used for advertising, and
       there is nothing here that could identify a person.</p>

    <h2>Who can see it</h2>
    <p><strong>Anyone who has your budget ID can read and change that budget.</strong>
       That is deliberate — it is how a budget is shared between a phone, a
       partner's phone, and this website. It also means the ID is the only thing
       protecting the budget, so treat it like a password and only give it to
       people you want in your budget.</p>
    <p>An invitation link is the safer way to let someone in, and it is safer
       precisely because it is not the ID: it works once, it stops working after
       seven days, and you can cancel it before it is used. A link that is
       forwarded or seen by the wrong person after that is worthless, which is not
       true of the ID.</p>
    <p>Data is not sold, rented, or shared with anyone else. Nobody has access to
       the server except its operator.</p>

    <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
    <p>On a privately operated server in Canada, in a PostgreSQL database.
       Traffic between your device and the server is encrypted with HTTPS.</p>

    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>Deleting an expense removes it from every device sharing the budget.
       Deleted rows are retained on the server for a period so that other
       devices can learn about the deletion when they next sync.</p>
    <p>Unused invitations are deleted once they expire, and used ones are cleared
       out as soon as another is created for the same budget.</p>
    <p>To delete a budget and everything in it, email the address below with the
       budget ID and it will be removed. Removing a budget from a single device
       (in the app's settings) leaves the budget itself intact for anyone else
       using it.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The app is not directed at children and collects nothing that would
       identify anyone.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions, or a deletion request:
       <a href="mailto:avens19@gmail.com">avens19@gmail.com</a></p>
</article>
